<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paisius of Hilendar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1722">1722</a>–<a href="/years/1773">1773</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Paisiy Hilendarski</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paisius of Hilendar was a Bulgarian monk of the Hilendar Monastery on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a> and a founder of the Bulgarian National Revival. In 1762 he completed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonic-bulgarian-history">Slavonic-Bulgarian History</a>, which celebrated medieval Bulgarian tsars and saints and urged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> to take pride in their language and past. Copied and circulated by hand, it inspired the later national awakening.</p></div>
